# Regression (Round XXIV Track A):
# The "zero-cost move" advice mechanism was deleted because it emitted
# invalid advice 100% of the time (D31 full-strict rejects `!` at any
# bare-param call site with E_OwnershipMismatch). This fixture is a
# POSITIVE CONTROL: `!` param callee + `!` at call site. Pre AND post
# fix: NO warning (verifies deletion didn't over-suppress a would-be-valid
# case — which per class analysis doesn't exist, so this is a control).
#
# POSITIVE CONTROL: pins mechanism-absence, not defect-absence. By class
# analysis this fixture cannot go RED against any real defect (no
# bare-param means the deleted producer's guard would have early-returned
# pre-fix). RED-verify path is artificial (add naked eprintln to any
# deleted emit-site scaffold → RED even for this fixture). Do NOT read
# a green as coverage of a real class.
#
# RED-verify: with the deletion applied, a temp `eprintln!("zero-cost move
# probe")` added early in `src/main.rs` build path made this fixture go
# RED (the helper detects the substring); removing the probe returned it
# to GREEN.

int sum(Vector[int] !xs):
    int total = 0
    for x in xs:
        total = total + x
    return total

void main():
    Vector[int] v = [1, 2, 3]
    int s = sum(!v)
    print(s)
